; Coverage scope for the Tier 1 80% gate (see config/pytest.ini's --cov-fail-under).
;
; Tier 2 (evaluation, red_teaming, monitoring) is now implemented and tested,
; so it counts against the gate like any other real code.
;
; What remains omitted is still unimplemented skeleton: the governance package
; and the Tier 3 security modules (data_security, access_control,
; audit_logging, compliance, threat_detection), where every function raises
; NotImplementedError. Counting those would either force throwaway
; NotImplementedError-assertion tests with no real signal, or force lowering
; the gate for code that has no logic to test yet.
;
; cockpit/testing/* is itself testing infrastructure/example code (fixtures,
; demo unit/integration/benchmark tests), not application logic -- also omitted.
[run]
omit =
    cockpit/governance/*
    cockpit/security/data_security.py
    cockpit/security/access_control.py
    cockpit/security/audit_logging.py
    cockpit/security/compliance.py
    cockpit/security/threat_detection.py
    cockpit/testing/*
